;; M4S slice 2 (docs/m4s-contract.md): the foundation-aware overlay verb
;; composing with struct heads -- the EDIT targets a plain table (hop,
;; int-typed rows, expressible inline) that is dynamic in a recursive
;; stratum, while the struct constructor hangs downstream in an acyclic
;; stratum of the same cone.  Deleting a direct assertion on hop takes
;; set-overlay-negative-dred (candidacy at apply: foundation lost with
;; surviving unfounded rec), the sweep collapses the unfounded closure,
;; and the downstream struct maintenance tombstones mk rows by id.
;;
;; With r0 = {(1,2), (2,3)}:
;;   hop = { (1,2) (2,3) (1,3) }          copies nonrec 1; (1,3) rec 1
;;   out/mk mirror hop                    3 interned ids
;; Asserting hop(3,1) directly completes the cycle: hop = all 9 pairs
;; over {1,2,3}, mk = 9 ids.  Retracting it: (3,1) loses its only
;; foundation at apply (rec support is unfounded), the sweep discards the
;; 6 unfounded rows and reseeds (1,3) from its surviving (1,2)+(2,3)
;; support; mk keeps 3 live ids + 6 tombstones.  Re-asserting hop(3,1)
;; relearns everything: all 9 ORIGINAL ids resurrect.

table (r0 int int)
table (hop int int)
struct (mk int int)
table (out mk)

rule
(r0 X Y)
-->
(hop X Y)

rule
(hop X Y)
(hop Y Z)
-->
(hop X Z)

rule
(hop X Y)
-->
(out (mk X Y))
